WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.868
A CIA director says the U.S.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.802
is confident

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.337
China is considering

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:07.340
providing lethal aid to Russia in its war

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.308
in Ukraine.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:08.708
William

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:09.342
Burns said

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:09.876
his agency

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.611
doesn't think a final decision

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.512
has been made yet.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.981
But China aid could include

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:15.782
providing Russia

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.484
with drones and ammunition.

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:18.785
And as the war grinds

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:19.919
into its second year,

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:20.887
now there's no

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:22.322
letting up in the fighting.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.223
Ukrainian officials

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:25.291
say there was extensive Russian

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.027
shelling along the front lines

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.194
in the last 24 hours,

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.330
including the area around back

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.898
more in the east.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.634
CNN's Alex Marquardt is in the Dnipro,

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:35.535
Ukraine.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.003
Alex, what can you tell us about

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.138
what's happening this weekend?

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:41.041
There Hi there, Fredricka.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.008
Well, some of the fiercest

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:42.375
fighting with

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:42.976
some of the heaviest

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.310
casualties on both sides

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.146
is taking place around the city of Balkh.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:46.679
Moved

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:47.647
our Russian forces

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:48.748
primarily from the Volga

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:49.516
mercenary group

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.418
to appear to be making gains.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:52.352
They claim that they have

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.787
taken several villages

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:56.089
north of the city of mud in an attempt

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.390
to encircle it.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.358
Ukrainian forces

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.226
say that they are standing their ground

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:03.096
in the face of intense Russian assaults.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:03.863
Now, Fred,

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.065
over the course of the past few months,

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.366
this fight has evolved

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.801
from a longer range battle

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.969
with artillery, tanks

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.105
and mortars to a much closer fight.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.240
Urban warfare in the city

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.842
with fighting street

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.577
to street, building to building.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:20.113
Now, there is no talk yet of surrendering

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:20.513
the city

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.448
on the Ukrainian side,

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:22.282
but President Lewinski

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.483
has softened his

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.751
his stance on that, saying

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:25.985
that he will not

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.487
fight to keep it at any cost

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:30.023
if it means everybody is going to die.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.458
Meanwhile, Fred,

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:34.461
as the second year of the war starts,

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.262
there is no indication

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.363
that President Putin

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.332
is softening his stance

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.401
that he plans on changing course

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.636
or that he plans to pull back or sit down

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.472
for any kinds of negotiations.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:47.407
The CIA director, Bill Burns, talked

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.676
about President Putin's mindset

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.711
earlier today on CBS News. Take a listen.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.381
I think Putin is

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.649
right now entirely

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.552
too confident of his ability to wear down

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.155
Ukraine to grind away.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:02.522
And that's

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.290
what he's giving every evidence

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.359
that he's determined to do right now.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.727
At some point,

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.195
he's going to have to face up

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.363
to increasing costs

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.164
as well

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.932
in coffins coming home to

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.634
some of the poorest parts of Russia.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.904
The cumulative economic damage to Russia

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:18.972
as well.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.640
Huge reputational damage.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.841
That's not exactly been

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.976
a great advertisement.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.511
For Russian arms sales.

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.246
So this is going to build over time.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:27.347
But right now,

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:28.214
the honest answer,

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:32.185
I think Putin is quite determined

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:33.920
And in terms of the economic cost

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:34.521
on Russia,

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:36.422
the European Union has just announced

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.491
its 10th round of sanctions

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.125
against Russia,

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.593
which President Zelenskiy has called

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.729
very powerful. Fredricka.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:44.764
Alex, the CIA director, also talked

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:48.468
about China and mentioned that Russia

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:49.669
and China

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:50.870
appear to be

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.671
working closer

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.706
together, as well as now Iran

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.508
being part of the picture.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:56.910
What more can you report

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.111
on from your vantage point?

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.414
Both China and Iran

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:02.949
potentially deepening their ties

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:03.449
with Russia

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.617
when it comes to this fight in Ukraine.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.084
The U.S.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.753
now warning publicly

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.755
that China is actively considering

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:09.722
sending lethal aid

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.390
so weapons

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.593
to Russia in order to be used in Ukraine.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.863
The CIA director says that no decision

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:17.664
has been made yet

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:18.932
by Chinese leadership,

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:19.832
that they have not seen

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.833
any shipments yet.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.669
But the Biden administration openly

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.037
warning China

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:25.638
that there would be consequences

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.040
if they decide to go down that road.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.042
The US ambassador to the United Nations

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.410
I think that that would be a red line

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.911
because it would be a significant boost

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.546
for Russia in this fight.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:37.016
Meanwhile, Iran appears to be poised

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:37.917
to be getting

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.352
help with their missile program

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.354
from Russia, according to Bill Burns.

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:42.388
That is something that they have long

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.022
sought and Russia

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.290
is also apparently

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.626
considering sending fighter jets to Iran.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:48.161
So that relationship

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:49.662
between Iran and Russia and Iran

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:50.463
has been sending

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.732
kamikaze drones and ammunition here

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:54.734
to the Russians in Ukraine.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.069
That relationship

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:59.339
deepening in a fast and disturbing way.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.573
Director Burns said.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:01.174
So let's discuss

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.742
all of this with retired

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:03.343
Lieutenant Colonel

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:04.544
Alexander Vindman, a former

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:05.878
director of European affairs

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:06.512
at the White House

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.381
National Security Council.

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:09.182
Colonel Vindman,

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.650
great to have you back on the program.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.151
We appreciate it.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.254
Well, let's begin with U.S.

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:15.188
intelligence believing

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:16.322
China may provide

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.890
lethal support to Russian

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.025
troops in Ukraine.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.961
What are your thoughts on that?

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.196
That sounds like that could lead

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:25.164
to a serious escalation

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:28.468
and some big problems for the Ukrainians.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.436
Thanks, Jim, for having me on again.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.471
It is a serious problem.

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.439
There's very few game changers

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.074
in this war at this point.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.342
Russia is not going to be able

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:39.245
to pull a rabbit out of a hat

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:42.515
domestically or even with kind of second

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:43.549
string partnerships

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:46.352
with regards to Iran or North Korea.

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:47.720
China, on the other hand,

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.388
with its massive

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:50.523
industrial base is a game changer.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.493
If the Ukrainians lose, if Russia

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.462
somehow managed, manages to snatch

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.231
the victory out of the jaws of defeat,

00:04:58.231 --> 00:04:59.932
it's going to be on the air

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.568
at the aid of the Chinese.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.637
And this is the danger of a long war,

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:05.238
a war

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.973
that's entering its second year,

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:09.108
a war that's started to spill over.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:09.375
First,

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:10.209
we heard of

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.177
Iranian support,

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:12.345
then the North Koreans

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:13.713
providing ammunition.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:14.781
Now, the Chinese,

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:16.082
the reason that these countries

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:16.816
are doing that

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:18.584
so is because they smell opportunity

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:19.886
and vulnerability.

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.688
They smell opportunity in that

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:23.623
Russia can still potentially pull

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:24.824
some success out of this.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.859
This will aid the authoritarian world

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.027
and these countries

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:30.430
own aspirations to establish their

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.499
their own kind of imperial projects,

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.936
secure territory on their boundaries.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:39.138
And it's actually a vulnerability because

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.774
erosion is deterring,

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:43.743
deterrence is eroding.

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:45.211
And the

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.447
these powers start to think that, well,

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.482
you know, what are the real costs here?

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:51.417
Some minor sanctions.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.352
In exchange,

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.354
we could really undermine

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:55.288
the strength of the Euro

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:57.023
Atlantic Alliance, the United States.

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.424
So this is the danger of a long war

00:05:58.424 --> 00:05:58.891
scenario.

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.126
And frankly, in part,

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.227
this is the result of

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:02.762
insufficient support from the West

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:03.930
to help compel

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.766
a short war and force Putin, who is yet

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:09.902
still determined to win in Ukraine,

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.305
but wouldn't be able to be so,

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:12.872
let's say,

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:13.573
optimistic

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:15.341
if his forces were consistently

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:16.776
being defeated on the battlefield.

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:18.444
Obama is an example.

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:19.912
And again, so far.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:20.546
Yeah.

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:21.614
And I want to ask you a little bit

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:22.849
more about what Putin is up to in

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:23.316
just a moment.

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:24.317
But let me ask you this,

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:25.451
because on China,

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:26.986
the South China Sea is one of the most

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:28.321
contested regions in the world.

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:30.123
As you know, Chinese fighter jets

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:31.491
will sometimes confront U.S.

00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:32.425
military aircraft.

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:33.760
And I think this gets to the point

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:34.961
you were just making a few moments ago

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:36.829
about spheres of influence.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:37.830
I just have to ask you about this.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:38.464
A CNN crew

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:39.065
was on board

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:40.032
a Navy plane

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:40.700
just recently

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.969
as one of these encounters unfolded

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:44.670
China is building up

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.205
its military presence there.

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:47.807
Tensions are simmering.

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:48.875
I mean, I remember

00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:49.275
covering this

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:50.143
when I covered

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:52.211
the Obama and Trump administrations.

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:53.846
Do you think

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:56.883
do you see this as potentially erupting

00:06:56.883 --> 00:06:59.018
into a military confrontation,

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:00.553
an actual military confrontation?

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:03.423
I think these

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.658
bumps in the South China Sea

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:08.461
are unlikely to result in broader

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:09.662
confrontations.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:10.463
I think there's a chance

00:07:10.463 --> 00:07:11.731
of accident, miscalculation.

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:13.533
The interests on both the Chinese

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:13.966
and the U.S.

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:15.735
part would be to avoid

00:07:15.735 --> 00:07:17.103
a broader spillover.

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:19.806
But the relationship is overall

00:07:19.806 --> 00:07:22.008
getting much, much sharper. The U.S.

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:24.977
destroying Russia's corruption, China's

00:07:25.845 --> 00:07:27.246
surveillance balloons.

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:28.848
That's a signal

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:29.615
that we are now

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:31.317
moving into a kind of a more acute

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:32.285
phase of the war.

00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:34.520
The Chinese, you know, really kind of

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:35.955
the timing is telling

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.323
that they're now considering providing

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:38.191
Russia aid

00:07:38.191 --> 00:07:38.991
is in part

00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:39.926
probably a response

00:07:39.926 --> 00:07:41.761
to this worsening relationship.

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:43.629
So we're not really in danger

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:45.598
of a confrontation immediately.

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:46.699
But if this relationship

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:48.901
keeps spiraling for another six months

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:50.470
or couple of years,

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:51.304
we could start to

00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:52.572
to really kind of shape

00:07:52.572 --> 00:07:53.172
an environment

00:07:53.172 --> 00:07:54.874
for a broader confrontation.

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:56.809
Instead, what we should be doing is

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:58.811
we should make sure that Russia

00:07:58.811 --> 00:07:59.879
loses in Ukraine,

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:02.548
and that depresses the ideas of China

00:08:02.682 --> 00:08:04.116
or any other country

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:05.284
pursuing a military means

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:06.118
to achieve their aims.

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:07.987
That is the biggest deterrence we have.

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:08.888
It's just that

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:11.090
this is war too long so far.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:11.691
Yeah.

00:08:11.691 --> 00:08:13.826
And that's why the Ukraine question

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:14.527
is so important.

00:08:14.527 --> 00:08:16.662
And getting back to that, Putin says,

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:16.963
you know,

00:08:16.963 --> 00:08:18.431
Russia can't ignore the nuclear

00:08:18.431 --> 00:08:19.632
capabilities of the U.S.

00:08:19.632 --> 00:08:21.000
and other NATO countries.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:21.501
You know, he's

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:23.703
obviously engaging in more of this

00:08:23.703 --> 00:08:25.338
nuclear bluster.

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:27.373
This is a question

00:08:27.373 --> 00:08:28.441
that comes up from time to time.

00:08:28.441 --> 00:08:28.975
Colonel Vindman,

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:31.811
what is your latest sense of this?

00:08:31.811 --> 00:08:33.446
Do we need to take this

00:08:33.446 --> 00:08:35.414
as any more than bluster?

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:36.949
Is there a darker message

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:37.984
in portraying Russia

00:08:37.984 --> 00:08:39.919
as facing this existential threat?

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:41.821
It obviously uses that for domestic

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:43.055
political purposes.

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:46.292
But should it be a concern for everybody?

00:08:46.292 --> 00:08:46.726
No.

00:08:46.726 --> 00:08:48.728
I think there will be a time where

00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:49.929
where this question

00:08:49.929 --> 00:08:52.532
of nuclear saber-rattling or nuclear

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:54.500
consideration of a nuclear option

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.768
might become life.

00:08:55.768 --> 00:08:57.203
It might become live,

00:08:57.203 --> 00:08:57.737
you know, a

00:08:57.737 --> 00:08:58.738
year down the road

00:08:58.738 --> 00:09:01.440
when after a series of failures

00:09:01.541 --> 00:09:03.175
on the part of the Russian ground forces

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:04.443
and Ukraine

00:09:04.443 --> 00:09:06.579
liberating additional territory.

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:08.748
Crimea comes under a real threat.

00:09:08.748 --> 00:09:09.949
And at that point in time,

00:09:09.949 --> 00:09:11.884
Putin is going to have to

00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:14.053
really start to think about what he does.

00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:16.055
Does he withdraw or does he take the loss

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:16.956
or does he escalate?

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:17.890
Ultimately, he's

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:19.392
not going to risk his regime

00:09:19.392 --> 00:09:20.960
by employing nuclear weapons

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:21.928
and being ostracized

00:09:21.928 --> 00:09:23.763
by the remaining allies he has.

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:25.097
Really that's China.

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:27.700
That's the kind of the nefarious actors.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:28.868
But also India

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:30.002
that would have to

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:32.104
then break contact with Russia.

00:09:32.738 --> 00:09:34.373
But that's when it gets dangerous

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:35.741
way down the line.

00:09:35.741 --> 00:09:36.842
What we should be doing,

00:09:36.842 --> 00:09:38.110
and I wrote about this recently, is

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.111
we should be giving Ukraine

00:09:39.111 --> 00:09:41.080
all the means they need to succeed

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.315
to liberate territory

00:09:42.315 --> 00:09:42.915
until he's

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:44.850
threatened the liberation of Crimea

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.652
that forces Putin negotiate.

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:48.688
That's when the that is

00:09:48.688 --> 00:09:49.322
do you think that

00:09:49.322 --> 00:09:50.222
not to cut you off there,

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:51.624
but does that include the F-16s?

00:09:52.658 --> 00:09:53.626
Absolutely.

00:09:53.626 --> 00:09:55.428
F-16s should be part of the mix.

00:09:55.428 --> 00:09:55.861
So should

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:56.362
the advanced

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:59.398
drones are reapers and Predator drones

00:09:59.665 --> 00:10:01.334
that have much, much greater legs

00:10:01.334 --> 00:10:02.368
than anything that the Ukrainians

00:10:02.368 --> 00:10:03.669
have in their inventory,

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:05.371
including firepower.

00:10:05.371 --> 00:10:06.339
Those should be going in.

00:10:06.339 --> 00:10:08.341
We should be not talking about

00:10:08.341 --> 00:10:10.876
30 Abrams tanks, but 300 Abrams tanks.

00:10:11.143 --> 00:10:12.578
The metering of equipment

00:10:12.578 --> 00:10:14.246
is playing out right now

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:16.849
on the geopolitical stage because, again,

00:10:16.849 --> 00:10:19.552
the Chinese perceive vulnerabilities.

00:10:19.552 --> 00:10:21.687
They perceive that they might be able

00:10:21.687 --> 00:10:23.089
to provide Ukraine,

00:10:23.089 --> 00:10:25.591
provide Russia with enough aid where

00:10:25.591 --> 00:10:27.093
Russia is successful in Ukraine.

00:10:27.093 --> 00:10:28.961
This is an erosion of deterrence.

00:10:28.961 --> 00:10:29.962
What we should be doing

00:10:29.962 --> 00:10:31.297
is providing Ukraine

00:10:31.297 --> 00:10:32.465
all the resources they need.

00:10:32.465 --> 00:10:34.033
So like this, deterrence becomes

00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:35.901
remains ironclad.

00:10:35.901 --> 00:10:36.702
And China

00:10:36.702 --> 00:10:38.771
doesn't consider some sort of adventures.

00:10:38.771 --> 00:10:39.939
Doesn't provoke the West.

00:10:39.939 --> 00:10:40.773
That's going to respond

00:10:40.773 --> 00:10:42.575
not with just with sanctions,

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:44.210
but frankly with other ways to

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:47.647
to contain Russian and Chinese advances.

